    <record name="UserScript"
            c:type="GjsifyWebView2UserScript"
            opaque="1"
            glib:type-name="GjsifyWebView2UserScript"
            glib:get-type="gjsify_webview2_user_script_get_type"
            c:symbol-prefix="user_script">
      <source-position filename="src/c/gjsify-webview2.h" line="187"/>
      <constructor name="new" c:identifier="gjsify_webview2_user_script_new">
        <doc xml:space="preserve"
             filename="src/c/gjsify-webview2.h"
             line="202">A NON-EMPTY LIST OF EITHER KIND MAKES THE SCRIPT REFUSED, with a warning, by
gjsify_webview2_user_content_manager_add_script(). WebView2's
`AddScriptToExecuteOnDocumentCreated` carries no URL filter, and injecting the
script anyway would run it on origins the caller excluded — the exact failure
a block list exists to prevent — so refusing narrows in the safe direction for
both list kinds. Porting darwin's in-script guard (the source wrapped in a
labelled block that tests the document's URL) is what closes this; it is
outside ADR 0035 decision 4's counted subset and is not in this build.

The patterns themselves are WebKitGTK's `scheme://host/path` shape and are
kept unparsed: nothing here reads them, so a spelling this backend would have
got wrong cannot be mistaken for one it honoured.</doc>
        <source-position filename="src/c/gjsify-webview2.h" line="225"/>
        <return-value transfer-ownership="full">
          <doc xml:space="preserve"
               filename="src/c/gjsify-webview2.h"
               line="223">a new script.</doc>
          <type name="UserScript" c:type="GjsifyWebView2UserScript*"/>
        </return-value>
        <parameters>
          <parameter name="source" transfer-ownership="none">
            <doc xml:space="preserve"
                 filename="src/c/gjsify-webview2.h"
                 line="204">the script source.</doc>
            <type name="utf8" c:type="const gchar*"/>
          </parameter>
          <parameter name="injected_frames" transfer-ownership="none">
            <doc xml:space="preserve"
                 filename="src/c/gjsify-webview2.h"
                 line="205">which frames to inject into.</doc>
            <type name="UserContentInjectedFrames"
                  c:type="GjsifyWebView2UserContentInjectedFrames"/>
          </parameter>
          <parameter name="injection_time" transfer-ownership="none">
            <doc xml:space="preserve"
                 filename="src/c/gjsify-webview2.h"
                 line="206">when to inject.</doc>
            <type name="UserScriptInjectionTime"
                  c:type="GjsifyWebView2UserScriptInjectionTime"/>
          </parameter>
          <parameter name="allow_list"
                     transfer-ownership="none"
                     nullable="1"
                     allow-none="1">
            <doc xml:space="preserve"
                 filename="src/c/gjsify-webview2.h"
                 line="207">URI patterns to allow, or %NULL for all.</doc>
            <array c:type="const gchar* const*">
              <type name="utf8" c:type="gchar*"/>
            </array>
          </parameter>
          <parameter name="block_list"
                     transfer-ownership="none"
                     nullable="1"
                     allow-none="1">
            <doc xml:space="preserve"
                 filename="src/c/gjsify-webview2.h"
                 line="208">URI patterns to block, or %NULL for none.</doc>
            <array c:type="const gchar* const*">
